---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/for/b2b-wholesale";
const title = "SMS apps for Shopify B2B wholesale: contact and account workflows";
const desc = "Choose around company access, reorder responsibility and rep follow-up. A phone number on an order does not identify the person authorized to buy for every company location.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/for">All store types</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-cyan-100">{desc}</p>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>Start with the company contact, not a consumer cart</h2>
      <p>Shopify models companies, locations and customer contacts separately. Its company-contact documentation describes location-specific roles and permissions. Build your messaging map around the buyer responsible for the relevant location; keep accounts-payable and receiving contacts out of promotional reorder segments unless they independently qualify. A shared company telephone number is a poor default audience key.</p>
      <h2>Approval is an access decision before it is a message</h2>
      <p>Shopify documents an approval notification email and a Flow template for approved B2B contacts. Use that existing owner as the baseline. An SMS app must not announce approval merely because a request form was submitted. Require the approved state and correct location access before considering an additional notification; keep promotional enrollment separate from account access.</p>
      <h2>Reorder reminders need a rep and quote exclusion</h2>
      <p>Use ordered case quantities and customer-specific reorder history as planning inputs, not a universal replenishment interval. Exclude accounts with an open quote, a negotiated renewal, an unresolved shipment or an assigned rep conversation. Decide who can release that exclusion. A bulk reorder link should lead to authenticated account pricing rather than put negotiated terms in a text that can be forwarded.</p>
      <h2>Proposed acceptance cases for a vendor demonstration</h2>
      <p>These are proposed checks, not completed tests. Create a company with two locations and different buyers. Approve only one buyer and confirm the other receives no approval message. Reassign the purchasing contact and confirm the old phone is excluded. Place a draft order with a rep and verify that an automated reorder prompt pauses. Repeat with a buyer who accepts email but has no SMS permission.</p>
      <h2>Evaluate the app against account data and reply ownership</h2>
      <p>Ask each SMS candidate to demonstrate the exact company/location fields it can receive, their update delay and what happens when a field is absent. A customer tag is not evidence of location-level access. Require a reply route to the responsible rep, an absence fallback and a way to pause automation during negotiation. Compare Postscript, Klaviyo, Omnisend or Attentive only after this demonstration; this page does not rank their B2B support.</p>
      <h2>Budget and measure at the account level</h2>
      <p>Track completed eligible reorders and margin after case discounts, freight, message charges and rep time. Count messages to every contact on an account, not only cost per phone. Compare a proposed reminder cohort with a comparable unmessaged cohort where feasible; rep-attributed revenue and SMS-attributed revenue may describe the same order. Record overlap rather than adding both totals.</p>
      <h2>Implementation and email coordination</h2>
      <p>Begin with an account-to-contact inventory, then one approval or reorder workflow with an assigned rep. Keep catalog updates, MOQ explanations and payment-term education in email. Sequenzy can remain an email shortlist candidate if its current integration can receive the required account states; do not assume native B2B support or a fixed price. Keep one owner for access notifications, one for promotions and a shared suppression record. Document channel permission, timezone handling, opt-out behavior and reply escalation before a pilot.</p>
      <h2>Primary reference and scope</h2>
      <p><a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/b2b/companies-and-customers/adding-customers">Shopify company contacts and approval notifications</a>. Checked November 25, 2026. This supports the platform behavior described above, not a live integration test or an app ranking. Channel permission and legal requirements depend on destination and message purpose; this page does not certify compliance.</p>
    </article>
    <p class="mt-10"><a class="link" href="/apps">Explore app reviews</a> · <a class="link" href="/guides/email-sms-coordination">Email and SMS coordination</a> · <a class="link" href="/guides/consent">Consent guide</a></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
